  "part_of_speech": "verb (godan, transitive)",
  "gloss": "to master (riding/driving); to handle skillfully",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to master (riding/driving); to handle skillfully",
      "explanation": "To become proficient at riding, driving, or operating something; to use something skillfully as if it were an extension of oneself."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "05741_norikonasu_ex1",
      "japanese": "{新|あたら}しい{車|くるま}を{乗|の}りこなす。",
      "english": "To master driving a new car.",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "05741_norikonasu_ex2",
      "japanese": "{彼|かれ}は{馬|うま}を{上手|じょうず}に{乗|の}りこなす。",
      "english": "He handles horses skillfully.",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "05741_norikonasu_ex3",
      "japanese": "このバイクを{乗|の}りこなすには{練習|れんしゅう}が{必要|ひつよう}だ。",
      "english": "It takes practice to master this motorcycle.",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "COMPOUND VERB:\n{乗|の}る (to ride) + こなす (to manage, handle skillfully)\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n{他動詞|たどうし} (transitive) - takes を\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {車|くるま}を{乗|の}りこなす: to master driving a car\n- {馬|うま}を{乗|の}りこなす: to handle horses well\n- バイクを{乗|の}りこなす: to master a motorcycle\n- スキーを{乗|の}りこなす: to ski skillfully\n\nEXTENDED MEANING:\nCan also mean to master using technology or tools:\n- 新しいソフトを{乗|の}りこなす: to master new software",
